  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Percentage of gender-specific proposals of policies and measures (as submitted by the regional Alliance of Women Anti-Corruption and Integrity Leaders) adopted by the national authorities.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2005">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0%</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">50%</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">67%
Participants in the regional meetings organized to set up the alliance proposed that 3 countries (Lebanon, Jordan, and Iraq) review the presence of gender perspectives in their national anti-corruption strategies and work to enhance these perspectives with view to reinforcing synergies with gender equality and women empowerment. 

Two of three countries (2/3) agreed to the proposed above: 

1.	Jordan reviewed the presence of gender perspectives in the national anti-corruption strategy and agreed to integrate gender dimensions in the 2023 operational plans of the national anti-corruption strategy.

2.	Lebanon agreed to initiate the review of gender perspectives then integrate gender dimensions and related indicators in the national anti-corruption strategy itself.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
